-- Issue 132: a CONTAINING region holds at most the largest encoding of its contents, and the contents end inside the
-- region, to the bit. --acn-v2 regions with an external size (POctExt, PBitExt, PBitExt2) were bounded only by the
-- rest of the stream: Ada read the fields after an over-long region past the end of the stream as zeros and returned
-- success with the position past the end, C accepted a region that left the following fields inside the stream and
-- skipped its unused part. BIT STRING contents that end past their region (BBox, PBitEmb: embedded length; PBitExt,
-- PBitExt2 in legacy: external size) were accepted by Ada (both modes) and by C legacy (contents ending inside the
-- region's last octet). The region around a CHOICE (010_choice.asn1, --acn-v2 only) is bounded by the CHOICE's own
-- maximum, not by its largest CONTAINING alternative.
-- No directives: run by v4Tests/scripts/runWireTests.sh with 010_decode_test.c / 010_decode_test.adb (C with ASan /
-- UBSan, Ada with -gnata), legacy and --acn-v2.
ACN-WIRE-REGION DEFINITIONS AUTOMATIC TAGS ::= BEGIN
    T        ::= SEQUENCE { a INTEGER (0..255), b BOOLEAN OPTIONAL, c INTEGER (0..255) OPTIONAL }
    Inner    ::= SEQUENCE { a INTEGER (0..255), b INTEGER (0..3) }
    BBox     ::= BIT STRING (CONTAINING T)
    OBox     ::= OCTET STRING (CONTAINING T)
    PBitEmb  ::= SEQUENCE { f BIT STRING (CONTAINING T), tail INTEGER (0..15) }
    PBitExt  ::= SEQUENCE { f BIT STRING (CONTAINING T), tail INTEGER (0..15) }
    POctExt  ::= SEQUENCE { v OCTET STRING (CONTAINING Inner), tail INTEGER (0..15) }
    PBitExt2 ::= SEQUENCE { v BIT STRING (CONTAINING Inner), tail INTEGER (0..15) }
END
